WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:03.490
I've been playing by the rules way too long.

00:00:03.490 --> 00:00:05.461
It's getting to a point of ridiculousness that

00:00:05.461 --> 00:00:08.380
I'm somehow responsible for the whole world around me

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:11.910
and I'm simply not and I'm unwilling to be.

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:13.510
We need to bend the curve.

00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:15.070
California Governor Gavin Newsom

00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:17.030
has imposed some of the most stringent

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:19.460
COVID-19 restrictions in America

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:22.220
and some golden state residents are starting to revolt.

00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:27.971
The dictatorial attitude toward California residents while dining in luxury, traveling, 

00:00:27.971 --> 00:00:32.610
keeping his business open and sending his kids to in-person private schools

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:36.000
is very telling about his attitude toward California residents,

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.840
and it is extremely hypocritical.

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:41.220
These closures and stay at home orders are flat out ridiculous.

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:45.540
Riverside County Sheriff, Chad Bianco released this video announcing that his department

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:47.920
wouldn't be enforcing the governor's order.

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:51.420
Sheriffs in Los Angeles County, El Dorado County, Orange County,

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:53.700
and even the governor's home of Sacramento County

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:57.350
have also said they will not enforce aspects of the lockdown order.

00:00:57.350 --> 00:01:00.460
Bianco says County sheriffs are acting within their legal authority.

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:02.130
We're constitutional officers.

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:03.280
Some of the sheriffs believe

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:05.520
that it's a constitutional violation.

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:07.920
We don't answer to a board of supervisors.

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:12.780
We don't answer to a governor, or to a city council.

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:16.740
We answer to the entire 2.5 million people of our county.

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:19.770
Do you worry that there's any sort of legal action

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:22.300
that can be taken against the department

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:26.040
for not following a governor's orders?

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:26.930
Yeah, no, there is not.

00:01:26.930 --> 00:01:29.740
We don't have to arrest just because there is a law.

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:32.330
On December 3rd, Newsom's stay at home order

00:01:32.330 --> 00:01:35.320
barred in-person dining of any kind at restaurants

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:39.330
where hospital ICU capacity has fallen below 15 percent,

00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:42.390
as it has in four of five California regions,

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:44.250
but there's no evidence that the shutdown

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:45.920
has stemmed the growth in cases,

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:48.620
hospital admissions, or fatalities.

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:52.120
Several restaurants in Riverside County are defying the ban,

00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:56.480
including Marla's Cocina and Cantina in the city of Beaumont.

00:01:56.480 --> 00:01:58.130
At this point with this shutdown

00:01:58.130 --> 00:02:00.220
we really have just kind of decided, listen,

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:02.140
I don't know how much more we can bend.

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:04.700
You don't like it, don't come.

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:08.970
A cantina started only accepting takeout orders for one week in March.

00:02:08.970 --> 00:02:11.970
The owner Diego Rose says never again.

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:15.230
I can't open up for just to-go's. I would be losing every day.

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:16.700
At that point, you have to make a decision.

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:20.460
Do you shut your doors and lose all your inventory,

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:22.410
and let your staff go,

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:25.480
in hopes that somebody along the way

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:26.537
knew what they were talking about,

00:02:26.537 --> 00:02:29.620
and that "two week flatten the curve" thing

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:31.590
was what they said?

00:02:31.590 --> 00:02:33.960
California's order to stop outdoor dining

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:37.770
has generated outrage, controversy, and legal challenges.

00:02:37.770 --> 00:02:41.000
A county judge invalidated the L.A. ban on the ground

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:44.470
that there's a lack of scientific evidence to justify it.

00:02:44.470 --> 00:02:47.710
Rose is even permitting his customers to dine in inside,

00:02:47.710 --> 00:02:49.390
though he's spaced out the tables

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:51.240
and installed extra ventilation.

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:54.900
He also spent about $35,000 converting an indoor space

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:56.270
into an open air patio,

00:02:56.270 --> 00:02:59.252
and keeps the restaurant doors open whenever possible.

00:02:59.252 --> 00:03:02.650
We have every option your little heart could desire.

00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:04.660
You want to sit outside, sit outside.

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:06.650
You want to sit in the patio, sit in the patio.

00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:08.690
You want to sit in a booth, sit in a booth.

00:03:08.690 --> 00:03:10.830
You want to sit on your thumb, sit on your thumb.

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:12.140
I'm not the world's keeper.

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:16.511
He says he's received visits from the Health Department, Alcohol and Beverage Control, 

00:03:16.511 --> 00:03:18.760
and angry citizens over the past several months,

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:22.740
and faced threats of fines for his patio not being COVID compliant.

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:24.920
But he remains committed to staying open,

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:28.320
and was emboldened by Sheriff Bianco's public statements.

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:31.520
To himself out there for the scrutiny

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:35.240
has definitely, I think, transcended the strength needed

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:39.900
for business people in all kinds of different capacities right now.

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:44.110
To say, hey listen, my sheriff has my back.

00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:47.850
But California is reaching record levels of COVID infections,

00:03:47.850 --> 00:03:50.650
and a new, more easily transmissible strain

00:03:50.650 --> 00:03:53.830
has appeared in the state, and in several California counties

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:57.170
hospitals are completely out of ICU capacity.

00:03:57.170 --> 00:03:59.850
What do you say to people who look at that situation

00:03:59.850 --> 00:04:03.450
and argue, you're creating a more dangerous situation

00:04:03.450 --> 00:04:06.130
by failing to discourage the spread of COVID?

00:04:06.130 --> 00:04:10.920
Making someone wear a mask or close their business,

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:12.960
that has absolutely nothing to do with

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:19.330
someone that is overweight, diabetic, unhealthy heart wise,

00:04:19.330 --> 00:04:22.074
possibly cancer, going through treatments,

00:04:22.074 --> 00:04:24.370
with a weak immune system,

00:04:24.370 --> 00:04:27.380
them going out into public and putting themselves at risk.

00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:29.450
That wasn't my fault.

00:04:29.450 --> 00:04:30.820
It had nothing to do with me.

00:04:30.820 --> 00:04:32.930
It had nothing to do with any other sheriff in the state,

00:04:32.930 --> 00:04:36.548
but no one wants to take personal responsibility.

00:04:36.548 --> 00:04:40.030
It's better if you blame someone else.

00:04:40.030 --> 00:04:42.440
There's little evidence that in-person dining,

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:46.550
particularly outdoors is a major source of COVID spread,

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:49.090
a fact the state's health director appeared to admit

00:04:49.090 --> 00:04:50.630
on a recent Zoom call.

00:04:50.630 --> 00:04:55.790
The decision to include among other sectors outdoor dining

00:04:55.790 --> 00:05:00.180
really has to do with the goal of trying to keep people at home.

00:05:00.180 --> 00:05:05.340
Not a comment on the relative safety of outdoor dining.

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:09.211
Research out of New York City found that 74 percent of COVID spread

00:05:09.211 --> 00:05:10.900
happens in households.

00:05:10.900 --> 00:05:13.450
Rose, who once worked as an emergency room nurse,

00:05:13.450 --> 00:05:14.840
says that the responsibility

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:17.670
for stopping the spread of COVID to the vulnerable

00:05:17.670 --> 00:05:20.750
doesn't rest with law enforcement or business owners.

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:24.703
Every individual has to keep and maintain

00:05:24.703 --> 00:05:27.440
the amount of risk they're willing to assume

00:05:27.440 --> 00:05:29.310
and that's inherent to the individual.

00:05:29.310 --> 00:05:30.910
California's stay at home order,

00:05:30.910 --> 00:05:32.560
prohibiting restaurants in counties

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:36.880
with available ICU capacity below 15% remains in effect.

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:39.780
A judge in San Diego County ruled that restaurants there

00:05:39.780 --> 00:05:43.177
can remain open pending a ruling in an ongoing lawsuit,

00:05:43.177 --> 00:05:45.570
and San Bernardino County has filed suit

00:05:45.570 --> 00:05:48.090
against the governor in the State's Supreme Court

00:05:48.090 --> 00:05:49.890
to keep its businesses open.

00:05:49.890 --> 00:05:51.610
Rose says he hopes more restaurants

00:05:51.610 --> 00:05:54.081
continue to ignore the order and reopen.

00:05:54.081 --> 00:05:55.850
I'm not worried about my business

00:05:55.850 --> 00:05:57.900
as much as I'm worried about my country.

00:05:57.900 --> 00:06:01.930
If I have nothing to open back up to, what's the point again?

00:06:01.930 --> 00:06:06.160
Freedom first, our choices are first, your choices are first

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:09.060
and I hope more and more people get on that kind of a bandwagon

00:06:09.060 --> 00:06:11.510
to protect each other's rights.

00:06:11.510 --> 00:06:13.413
We have to, we have to do something.

